# dist/ is a build artifact versioned on purpose — Electron loads it at runtime,
# so the app must run from a bare clone. That only holds if the bytes here are
# the bytes Vite produced.
#
# Without this, git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, the default) rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout. The next `npm run build` writes LF back, and dist/ shows as
# modified — which blocks `git pull` on any machine that has run setup.bat,
# naming files the user never edited.
#
# This file lives beside dist/, not inside it: `vite build` empties the output
# directory, so a .gitattributes placed within dist/ is deleted by every build.
dist/** -text
